{"id":"mahabharata-6-043","work":"mahabharata","part":6,"partName":"भीष्मपर्व","partNameEn":"Bhishma Parva","unit":43,"title":"त्रिचत्वारिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 43 · First day: the morning fighting","summary":{"en":"The terrible morning battle begins, with kings hacking each other down and Bhishma and Abhimanyu fighting like Indra and Bali. Warriors on both sides fall in great numbers.","kn":"ಭಯಂಕರ ಬೆಳಗಿನ ಯುದ್ಧ ಆರಂಭವಾಗುತ್ತದೆ; ರಾಜರು ಒಬ್ಬರನ್ನೊಬ್ಬರು ಕಡಿಯುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಮತ್ತು ಅಭಿಮನ್ಯು ಇಂದ್ರ ಬಲಿಯರಂತೆ ಹೋರಾಡುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಎರಡೂ ಕಡೆ ಅನೇಕ ಯೋಧರು ಬೀಳುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"भयंकर प्रातःकालीन युद्ध आरम्भ होता है; राजा एक-दूसरे को काटते हैं और भीष्म तथा अभिमन्यु इन्द्र और बलि की तरह लड़ते हैं। दोनों ओर बहुत से योद्धा गिरते हैं।","te":"భయంకరమైన ఉదయపు యుద్ధం మొదలవుతుంది; రాజులు ఒకరినొకరు నరుక్కుంటారు. భీష్ముడు, అభిమన్యుడు ఇంద్ర బలుల్లా పోరాడతారు; ఇరుపక్షాల్లో అనేకులు పడిపోతారు.","ta":"கொடிய காலைப் போர் தொடங்குகிறது; மன்னர்கள் ஒருவரை ஒருவர் வெட்டுகின்றனர். பீஷ்மரும் அபிமன்யுவும் இந்திரனும் பலியும் போல் போரிடுகின்றனர்; இரு தரப்பிலும் பலர் வீழ்கின்றனர்.","ml":"പ്രഭാതയുദ്ധം ഭയങ്കരമായി തുടങ്ങുന്നു; രാജാക്കന്മാർ പരസ്പരം വെട്ടിവീഴ്ത്തുന്നു, ഭീഷ്മരും അഭിമന്യുവും ഇന്ദ്രനും ബലിയും പോലെ പോരാടുന്നു. ഇരുപക്ഷത്തും യോദ്ധാക്കൾ വലിയ തോതിൽ വീഴുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 6.43; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 26 2021","sections":[{"title":"भीष्मवधपर्व","titleEn":"Bhishmavadha Parva (The fall of Bhishma)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"पूर्वाह्णे तस्य रौद्रस्य युद्धमह्नो विशां पते ।\nप्रावर्तत महाघोरं राज्ञां देहावकर्तनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the morning of that dreadful day, lord of the people, a terrible battle began, in which the bodies of kings were hacked apart."}},{"n":2,"text":"कुरूणां पाण्डवानां च संग्रामे विजिगीषताम् ।\nसिंहानामिव संह्रादो दिवमुर्वीं च नादयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The roar of the Kurus and Pandavas, each eager to win, was like the roaring of lions, and made sky and earth resound."}},{"n":3,"text":"आसीत्किलकिलाशब्दस्तलशङ्खरवैः सह ।\nजज्ञिरे सिंहनादाश्च शूराणां प्रतिगर्जताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There were shouts, with the sound of clapping and conches, and the lion-roars of heroes answering each other's challenges."}},{"n":4,"text":"तलत्राभिहताश्चैव ज्याशब्दा भरतर्षभ ।\nपत्तीनां पादशब्दाश्च वाजिनां च महास्वनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There were twangs of bowstrings struck against the arm-guards, best of the Bharatas, the tramp of foot soldiers and the loud neighing of horses."}},{"n":5,"text":"तोत्त्राङ्कुशनिपाताश्च आयुधानां च निस्वनाः ।\nघण्टाशब्दाश्च नागानामन्योन्यमभिधावताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There were the falls of goads and prods, the clash of weapons, and the bells of elephants charging at one another."}},{"n":6,"text":"तस्मिन्समुदिते शब्दे तुमुले लोमहर्षणे ।\nबभूव रथनिर्घोषः पर्जन्यनिनदोपमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Amid that rising terrifying, hair-raising noise, the rumble of chariots sounded like thunder from a rain-cloud."}},{"n":7,"text":"ते मनः क्रूरमाधाय समभित्यक्तजीविताः ।\nपाण्डवानभ्यवर्तन्त सर्व एवोच्छ्रितध्वजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Resolving on cruelty and ready to give up their lives, all of them, with banners raised, advanced against the Pandavas."}},{"n":8,"text":"स्वयं शांतनवो राजन्नभ्यधावद्धनंजयम् ।\nप्रगृह्य कार्मुकं घोरं कालदण्डोपमं रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shantanu's son Bhishma himself, O king, rushed at Arjuna, taking up a dreadful bow like the staff of Death."}},{"n":9,"text":"अर्जुनोऽपि धनुर्गृह्य गाण्डीवं लोकविश्रुतम् ।\nअभ्यधावत तेजस्वी गाङ्गेयं रणमूर्धनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna too, taking up his world-famous bow Gandiva, rushed in his radiance at Ganga's son at the head of the battle."}},{"n":10,"text":"तावुभौ कुरुशार्दूलौ परस्परवधैषिणौ ।\nगाङ्गेयस्तु रणे पार्थं विद्ध्वा नाकम्पयद्बली ।\nतथैव पाण्डवो राजन्भीष्मं नाकम्पयद्युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those two tigers of the Kurus, each seeking the other's death, met. The mighty son of Ganga pierced Partha in battle but did not shake him, and likewise the Pandava, O king, did not shake Bhishma."}},{"n":11,"text":"सात्यकिश्च महेष्वासः कृतवर्माणमभ्ययात् ।\nतयोः समभवद्युद्धं तुमुलं लोमहर्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great archer Satyaki advanced on Kritavarman, and a tumultuous, hair-raising fight arose between them."}},{"n":12,"text":"सात्यकिः कृतवर्माणं कृतवर्मा च सात्यकिम् ।\nआनर्छतुः शरैर्घोरैस्तक्षमाणौ परस्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Satyaki and Kritavarman struck each other with dreadful arrows, each cutting at the other."}},{"n":13,"text":"तौ शराचितसर्वाङ्गौ शुशुभाते महाबलौ ।\nवसन्ते पुष्पशबलौ पुष्पिताविव किंशुकौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their bodies covered with arrows, those two mighty men shone like flowering kimshuka trees in spring, speckled with blossoms."}},{"n":14,"text":"अभिमन्युर्महेष्वासो बृहद्बलमयोधयत् ।\nततः कोसलको राजा सौभद्रस्य विशां पते ।\nध्वजं चिच्छेद समरे सारथिं च न्यपातयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great archer Abhimanyu fought Brihadbala. Then the king of Kosala cut down Subhadra's son's banner and struck his charioteer down in the battle, O lord of the people."}},{"n":15,"text":"सौभद्रस्तु ततः क्रुद्धः पातिते रथसारथौ ।\nबृहद्बलं महाराज विव्याध नवभिः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, angry that his charioteer had been felled, the son of Subhadra pierced Brihadbala with nine arrows, great king."}},{"n":16,"text":"अथापराभ्यां भल्लाभ्यां पीताभ्यामरिमर्दनः ।\nध्वजमेकेन चिच्छेद पार्ष्णिमेकेन सारथिम् ।\nअन्योन्यं च शरैस्तीक्ष्णैः क्रुद्धौ राजंस्ततक्षतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The crusher of foes then cut down Brihadbala's banner with one sharp yellow-bright broad-headed arrow and killed his charioteer's helper with another, and the two, enraged, wounded each other with keen arrows, O king."}},{"n":17,"text":"मानिनं समरे दृप्तं कृतवैरं महारथम् ।\nभीमसेनस्तव सुतं दुर्योधनमयोधयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena fought your son Duryodhana, a proud and arrogant great chariot-warrior with whom he had an old enmity."}},{"n":18,"text":"तावुभौ नरशार्दूलौ कुरुमुख्यौ महाबलौ ।\nअन्योन्यं शरवर्षाभ्यां ववृषाते रणाजिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those two tigers among men, great and mighty chiefs of the Kurus, rained showers of arrows on each other in the arena of battle."}},{"n":19,"text":"तौ तु वीक्ष्य महात्मानौ कृतिनौ चित्रयोधिनौ ।\nविस्मयः सर्वभूतानां समपद्यत भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing those two high-souled, skilled, wonderfully fighting warriors, all beings were filled with wonder, O Bharata."}},{"n":20,"text":"दुःशासनस्तु नकुलं प्रत्युद्याय महारथम् ।\nअविध्यन्निशितैर्बाणैर्बहुभिर्मर्मभेदिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duhshasana went against the great chariot-warrior Nakula and pierced him with many sharp arrows that tear the vital parts."}},{"n":21,"text":"तस्य माद्रीसुतः केतुं सशरं च शरासनम् ।\nचिच्छेद निशितैर्बाणैः प्रहसन्निव भारत ।\nअथैनं पञ्चविंशत्या क्षुद्रकाणां समार्दयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Madri's son, almost laughing, cut down his banner and his bow with sharp arrows, O Bharata, and then struck him with twenty-five small arrows."}},{"n":22,"text":"पुत्रस्तु तव दुर्धर्षो नकुलस्य महाहवे ।\nयुगेषां चिच्छिदे बाणैर्ध्वजं चैव न्यपातयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your unyielding son, in that great battle, cut the yoke-pegs of Nakula's chariot with arrows and brought his banner down."}},{"n":23,"text":"दुर्मुखः सहदेवं तु प्रत्युद्याय महाबलम् ।\nविव्याध शरवर्षेण यतमानं महाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Durmukha, advancing on the mighty Sahadeva, pierced him with a rain of arrows as he strove in the great fight."}},{"n":24,"text":"सहदेवस्ततो वीरो दुर्मुखस्य महाहवे ।\nशरेण भृशतीक्ष्णेन पातयामास सारथिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The hero Sahadeva then, in that great battle, felled Durmukha's charioteer with a very sharp arrow."}},{"n":25,"text":"तावन्योन्यं समासाद्य समरे युद्धदुर्मदौ ।\nत्रासयेतां शरैर्घोरैः कृतप्रतिकृतैषिणौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those two, meeting in battle, maddened by war, each wanting to repay the other, terrified each other with dreadful arrows."}},{"n":26,"text":"युधिष्ठिरः स्वयं राजा मद्रराजानमभ्ययात् ।\nतस्य मद्राधिपश्चापं द्विधा चिच्छेद मारिष ॥","meaning":{"en":"King Yudhishthira himself went against the king of Madra, Shalya, and the lord of Madra cut his bow in two, my lord."}},{"n":27,"text":"तदपास्य धनुश्छिन्नं कुन्तीपुत्रो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nअन्यत्कार्मुकमादाय वेगवद्बलवत्तरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Throwing aside the broken bow, Yudhishthira, son of Kunti, took another, swifter and stronger."}},{"n":28,"text":"ततो मद्रेश्वरं राजा शरैः संनतपर्वभिः ।\nछादयामास संक्रुद्धस्तिष्ठ तिष्ठेति चाब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then in anger the king covered the lord of Madra with straight-jointed arrows and called out, \"Stand, stand!\""}},{"n":29,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नस्ततो द्रोणमभ्यद्रवत भारत ।\nतस्य द्रोणः सुसंक्रुद्धः परासुकरणं दृढम् ।\nत्रिधा चिच्छेद समरे यतमानस्य कार्मुकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhrishtadyumna then rushed at Drona, O Bharata. Drona, furious, cut the strong bow of his striving foe into three pieces in battle, a bow that could end lives."}},{"n":30,"text":"शरं चैव महाघोरं कालदण्डमिवापरम् ।\nप्रेषयामास समरे सोऽस्य काये न्यमज्जत ॥","meaning":{"en":"He also sent a dreadful arrow, like a second staff of Death, which sank into Dhrishtadyumna's body."}},{"n":31,"text":"अथान्यद्धनुरादाय सायकांश्च चतुर्दश ।\nद्रोणं द्रुपदपुत्रस्तु प्रतिविव्याध संयुगे ।\nतावन्योन्यं सुसंक्रुद्धौ चक्रतुः सुभृशं रणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the son of Drupada took another bow and fourteen arrows and pierced Drona in return. Both enraged, those two fought a violent fight."}},{"n":32,"text":"सौमदत्तिं रणे शङ्खो रभसं रभसो युधि ।\nप्रत्युद्ययौ महाराज तिष्ठ तिष्ठेति चाब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the battle Shankha went against Somadatta's son, Bhurishravas, the fierce against the fierce, O great king, saying, \"Stand, stand!\""}},{"n":33,"text":"तस्य वै दक्षिणं वीरो निर्बिभेद रणे भुजम् ।\nसौमदत्तिस्तथा शङ्खं जत्रुदेशे समाहनत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The hero pierced Shankha's right arm in the fight, and Somadatta's son struck Shankha on the collarbone."}},{"n":34,"text":"तयोः समभवद्युद्धं घोररूपं विशां पते ।\nदृप्तयोः समरे तूर्णं वृत्रवासवयोरिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"A fearful battle took place between those two, lord of the people, like the fight between the proud Vritra and Indra."}},{"n":35,"text":"बाह्लीकं तु रणे क्रुद्धं क्रुद्धरूपो विशां पते ।\nअभ्यद्रवदमेयात्मा धृष्टकेतुर्महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhrishtaketu, the great chariot-warrior of immeasurable spirit, in a fury himself, rushed at the angry Bahlika in battle."}},{"n":36,"text":"बाह्लीकस्तु ततो राजन्धृष्टकेतुममर्षणम् ।\nशरैर्बहुभिरानर्छत्सिंहनादमथानदत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bahlika then struck the wrathful Dhrishtaketu with many arrows and roared a lion's roar."}},{"n":37,"text":"चेदिराजस्तु संक्रुद्धो बाह्लीकं नवभिः शरैः ।\nविव्याध समरे तूर्णं मत्तो मत्तमिव द्विपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king of the Chedis, enraged, quickly pierced Bahlika with nine arrows in battle, as one rutting elephant attacks another."}},{"n":38,"text":"तौ तत्र समरे क्रुद्धौ नर्दन्तौ च मुहुर्मुहुः ।\nसमीयतुः सुसंक्रुद्धावङ्गारकबुधाविव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Furious, bellowing again and again, they came together in battle like the planets Mars and Mercury."}},{"n":39,"text":"राक्षसं क्रूरकर्माणं क्रूरकर्मा घटोत्कचः ।\nअलम्बुसं प्रत्युदियाद्बलं शक्र इवाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ghatotkacha, cruel in his deeds, went against the cruel rakshasa Alambusa, as Indra went against Bala."}},{"n":40,"text":"घटोत्कचस्तु संक्रुद्धो राक्षसं तं महाबलम् ।\nनवत्या सायकैस्तीक्ष्णैर्दारयामास भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ghatotkacha, enraged, tore that mighty rakshasa with ninety sharp arrows, O Bharata."}},{"n":41,"text":"अलम्बुसस्तु समरे भैमसेनिं महाबलम् ।\nबहुधा वारयामास शरैः संनतपर्वभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Alambusa in turn held back Bhima's mighty son in battle in many ways with straight-jointed arrows."}},{"n":42,"text":"व्यभ्राजेतां ततस्तौ तु संयुगे शरविक्षतौ ।\nयथा देवासुरे युद्धे बलशक्रौ महाबलौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wounded by arrows in the fight, those two shone, like the mighty Bala and Indra in the war of gods and asuras."}},{"n":43,"text":"शिखण्डी समरे राजन्द्रौणिमभ्युद्ययौ बली ।\nअश्वत्थामा ततः क्रुद्धः शिखण्डिनमवस्थितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The strong Shikhandi advanced against Drona's son in battle, O king. Then Ashvatthama, enraged, stood before Shikhandi,"}},{"n":44,"text":"नाराचेन सुतीक्ष्णेन भृशं विद्ध्वा व्यकम्पयत् ।\nशिखण्ड्यपि ततो राजन्द्रोणपुत्रमताडयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"struck him hard with a very sharp iron arrow and made him tremble. Shikhandi too then struck Drona's son, O king,"}},{"n":45,"text":"सायकेन सुपीतेन तीक्ष्णेन निशितेन च ।\nतौ जघ्नतुस्तदान्योन्यं शरैर्बहुविधैर्मृधे ॥","meaning":{"en":"with a sharp, whetted, bright arrow. Each of them struck the other in the battle with many kinds of arrows."}},{"n":46,"text":"भगदत्तं रणे शूरं विराटो वाहिनीपतिः ।\nअभ्ययात्त्वरितो राजंस्ततो युद्धमवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Virata, leader of the army, quickly advanced against the heroic Bhagadatta in battle, O king, and then the fight began."}},{"n":47,"text":"विराटो भगदत्तेन शरवर्षेण ताडितः ।\nअभ्यवर्षत्सुसंक्रुद्धो मेघो वृष्ट्या इवाचलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Virata, struck by Bhagadatta's rain of arrows, in a fury showered him in return, as a cloud rains on a mountain."}},{"n":48,"text":"भगदत्तस्ततस्तूर्णं विराटं पृथिवीपतिम् ।\nछादयामास समरे मेघः सूर्यमिवोदितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhagadatta quickly covered King Virata in battle, as a cloud covers the risen sun."}},{"n":49,"text":"बृहत्क्षत्रं तु कैकेयं कृपः शारद्वतो ययौ ।\nतं कृपः शरवर्षेण छादयामास भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kripa, son of Sharadvat, went against Brihatkshatra of Kekaya, and Kripa covered him with a shower of arrows, O Bharata."}},{"n":50,"text":"गौतमं केकयः क्रुद्धः शरवृष्ट्याभ्यपूरयत् ।\nतावन्योन्यं हयान्हत्वा धनुषी विनिकृत्य वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Kekaya, angry, flooded Gautama Kripa with arrows. Having killed each other's horses and cut each other's bows,"}},{"n":51,"text":"विरथावसियुद्धाय समीयतुरमर्षणौ ।\nतयोस्तदभवद्युद्धं घोररूपं सुदारुणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"both, now without chariots, closed in with swords, each full of rage. A dreadful and very cruel fight arose between them."}},{"n":52,"text":"द्रुपदस्तु ततो राजा सैन्धवं वै जयद्रथम् ।\nअभ्युद्ययौ संप्रहृष्टो हृष्टरूपं परंतप ॥","meaning":{"en":"King Drupada then went joyfully against Jayadratha, the king of Sindhu, who also was in high spirits, O scorcher of foes."}},{"n":53,"text":"ततः सैन्धवको राजा द्रुपदं विशिखैस्त्रिभिः ।\nताडयामास समरे स च तं प्रत्यविध्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the king of Sindhu struck Drupada with three arrows in battle, and Drupada struck him back."}},{"n":54,"text":"तयोः समभवद्युद्धं घोररूपं सुदारुणम् ।\nईक्षितृप्रीतिजननं शुक्राङ्गारकयोरिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"A terrible and very cruel fight took place between them, as pleasing to onlookers as the meeting of Venus and Mars."}},{"n":55,"text":"विकर्णस्तु सुतस्तुभ्यं सुतसोमं महाबलम् ।\nअभ्ययाज्जवनैरश्वैस्ततो युद्धमवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your son Vikarna went with swift horses against the mighty Sutasoma, and then the fight began."}},{"n":56,"text":"विकर्णः सुतसोमं तु विद्ध्वा नाकम्पयच्छरैः ।\nसुतसोमो विकर्णं च तदद्भुतमिवाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vikarna pierced Sutasoma with arrows but could not shake him, nor could Sutasoma shake Vikarna. That was wonderful."}},{"n":57,"text":"सुशर्माणं नरव्याघ्रं चेकितानो महारथः ।\nअभ्यद्रवत्सुसंक्रुद्धः पाण्डवार्थे पराक्रमी ॥","meaning":{"en":"The valiant great chariot-warrior Chekitana, in great fury, rushed on Susharma, the tiger among men, for the Pandavas' sake."}},{"n":58,"text":"सुशर्मा तु महाराज चेकितानं महारथम् ।\nमहता शरवर्षेण वारयामास संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Susharma, great king, held the great chariot-fighter Chekitana back with a great shower of arrows in battle."}},{"n":59,"text":"चेकितानोऽपि संरब्धः सुशर्माणं महाहवे ।\nप्राच्छादयत्तमिषुभिर्महामेघ इवाचलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Chekitana, too, in a fury, covered Susharma with arrows in that great fight, as a great cloud covers a mountain."}},{"n":60,"text":"शकुनिः प्रतिविन्ध्यं तु पराक्रान्तं पराक्रमी ।\nअभ्यद्रवत राजेन्द्र मत्तो मत्तमिव द्विपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shakuni, a valiant fighter, rushed at the valiant Prativindhya, O king of kings, as a rutting elephant at another."}},{"n":61,"text":"यौधिष्ठिरस्तु संक्रुद्धः सौबलं निशितैः शरैः ।\nव्यदारयत संग्रामे मघवानिव दानवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira's son, enraged, tore Subala's son Shakuni with sharp arrows in the fight, as Indra tears a danava."}},{"n":62,"text":"शकुनिः प्रतिविन्ध्यं तु प्रतिविध्यन्तमाहवे ।\nव्यदारयन्महाप्राज्ञः शरैः संनतपर्वभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And the wise Shakuni tore Prativindhya, who was striking back in battle, with straight-jointed arrows."}},{"n":63,"text":"सुदक्षिणं तु राजेन्द्र काम्बोजानां महारथम् ।\nश्रुतकर्मा पराक्रान्तमभ्यद्रवत संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shrutakarma, valiant, rushed in battle at Sudakshina, the valiant great chariot-warrior of the Kambojas, O king of kings."}},{"n":64,"text":"सुदक्षिणस्तु समरे साहदेविं महारथम् ।\nविद्ध्वा नाकम्पयत वै मैनाकमिव पर्वतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sudakshina pierced Sahadeva's son, the great chariot-warrior, but could not shake him, as one cannot shake the mountain Mainaka."}},{"n":65,"text":"श्रुतकर्मा ततः क्रुद्धः काम्बोजानां महारथम् ।\nशरैर्बहुभिरानर्छद्दारयन्निव सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shrutakarma then, angry, struck the Kamboja great chariot-warrior with many arrows, as if splitting him on every side."}},{"n":66,"text":"इरावानथ संक्रुद्धः श्रुतायुषममर्षणम् ।\nप्रत्युद्ययौ रणे यत्तो यत्तरूपतरं ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Iravan, enraged and intent, advanced in the battle against the angry Shrutayu, who was even more intent."}},{"n":67,"text":"आर्जुनिस्तस्य समरे हयान्हत्वा महारथः ।\nननाद सुमहन्नादं तत्सैन्यं प्रत्यपूरयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna's son, the great chariot-warrior, killed Shrutayu's horses in the fight and gave a great roar that filled his own army."}},{"n":68,"text":"श्रुतायुस्त्वथ संक्रुद्धः फाल्गुनेः समरे हयान् ।\nनिजघान गदाग्रेण ततो युद्धमवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shrutayu, furious, killed the horses of Phalguna's son in the battle with the tip of his mace, and then the fighting went on."}},{"n":69,"text":"विन्दानुविन्दावावन्त्यौ कुन्तिभोजं महारथम् ।\nससेनं ससुतं वीरं संससज्जतुराहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"The two Avantis, Vinda and Anuvinda, engaged in battle the great chariot-warrior Kuntibhoja, a hero, with his army and his son."}},{"n":70,"text":"तत्राद्भुतमपश्याम आवन्त्यानां पराक्रमम् ।\nयदयुध्यन्स्थिरा भूत्वा महत्या सेनया सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"There we saw a wonderful display of valor by the Avantis, who fought steadily with a great army."}},{"n":71,"text":"अनुविन्दस्तु गदया कुन्तिभोजमताडयत् ।\nकुन्तिभोजस्ततस्तूर्णं शरव्रातैरवाकिरत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Anuvinda struck Kuntibhoja with a mace, and Kuntibhoja quickly showered him with swarms of arrows."}},{"n":72,"text":"कुन्तिभोजसुतश्चापि विन्दं विव्याध सायकैः ।\nस च तं प्रतिविव्याध तदद्भुतमिवाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kuntibhoja's son also pierced Vinda with arrows, and Vinda pierced him back. That was wonderful."}},{"n":73,"text":"केकया भ्रातरः पञ्च गान्धारान्पञ्च मारिष ।\nससैन्यास्ते ससैन्यांश्च योधयामासुराहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"The five Kekaya brothers, my lord, and the five Gandharas, each with their troops, fought one another in battle."}},{"n":74,"text":"वीरबाहुश्च ते पुत्रो वैराटिं रथसत्तमम् ।\nउत्तरं योधयामास विव्याध निशितैः शरैः ।\nउत्तरश्चापि तं धीरं विव्याध निशितैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your son Virabahu fought Uttara, the son of Virata and best of charioteers, and pierced him with sharp arrows, and Uttara pierced that steadfast one with sharp arrows too."}},{"n":75,"text":"चेदिराट्समरे राजन्नुलूकं समभिद्रवत् ।\nउलूकश्चापि तं बाणैर्निशितैर्लोमवाहिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king of the Chedis, O king, rushed at Uluka in battle, and Uluka struck him back with sharp arrows tipped with feathers."}},{"n":76,"text":"तयोर्युद्धं समभवद्घोररूपं विशां पते ।\nदारयेतां सुसंक्रुद्धावन्योन्यमपराजितौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"A terrible and very cruel fight arose between them, lord of the people. Furious and unconquered, they tore at one another."}},{"n":77,"text":"एवं द्वंद्वसहस्राणि रथवारणवाजिनाम् ।\nपदातीनां च समरे तव तेषां च संकुलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus there were thousands of duels of chariots, elephants and horses and of foot soldiers, in the crowded battle of your side and theirs."}},{"n":78,"text":"मुहूर्तमिव तद्युद्धमासीन्मधुरदर्शनम् ।\nतत उन्मत्तवद्राजन्न प्राज्ञायत किंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"For a moment the battle was pleasant to watch. Then, O king, it became like madness, and nothing could be made out."}},{"n":79,"text":"गजो गजेन समरे रथी च रथिनं ययौ ।\nअश्वोऽश्वं समभिप्रेत्य पदातिश्च पदातिनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Elephant went against elephant, chariot-warrior against chariot-warrior, horse against horse, and foot soldier against foot soldier."}},{"n":80,"text":"ततो युद्धं सुदुर्धर्षं व्याकुलं समपद्यत ।\nशूराणां समरे तत्र समासाद्य परस्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the very fierce battle became confused, as the heroes met one another in the fight."}},{"n":81,"text":"तत्र देवर्षयः सिद्धाश्चारणाश्च समागताः ।\nप्रैक्षन्त तद्रणं घोरं देवासुररणोपमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the divine sages, siddhas and charanas gathered and watched that dreadful battle, like the war of gods and asuras."}},{"n":82,"text":"ततो दन्तिसहस्राणि रथानां चापि मारिष ।\nअश्वौघाः पुरुषौघाश्च विपरीतं समाययुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then thousands of elephants and chariots, and masses of horses and of men, came together in reverse order, O my lord."}},{"n":83,"text":"तत्र तत्रैव दृश्यन्ते रथवारणपत्तयः ।\nसादिनश्च नरव्याघ्र युध्यमाना मुहुर्मुहुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here and there chariots, elephants, foot soldiers and horsemen were seen fighting again and again, tiger among men."}}]}]}